From 089df01bfa91c63e22cb5094dc6b6cdb5d3472d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:05:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X1: PCI identity + register file

Phase X1 of docs/plans/XHCI_PLAN.md: the controller exists on the bus.

PCI 0:20.0 carries the QEMU qemu-xhci identity (1b36:000d rev 01,
class 0x0C/0x03/0x30, subsystem 1af4:1100, INTA# on the measured-free
IRQ 10 -- in use: 0 PIT, 1 KBC, 8 RTC, 11 e1000, 14/15 AHCI, and
EHCI/UHCI drive no PIC line).  BAR0 is a 64-bit 64 KiB MMIO window
seeded at 0xFEB20000 (measured clear of EHCI 0xFEB00000, AHCI
0xFEB10000/0xFEB12000, e1000 0xFEBC0000) with the AHCI BAR5 pattern
for the sizing probe (0xFFFF0004) and firmware-relocation rebind.

src/xhci.c models the full register file against the measured guest
contract (XHCI_PLAN section 1a): the capability block (dword
0x01000040; HCSPARAMS1 32 slots / 1 interrupter / 4 ports;
HCSPARAMS2=0 so the guest skips scratchpads; HCCPARAMS1 AC64 with
CSZ=0/PPC=0; DBOFF 0x1000, RTSOFF 0x800), operational registers with
the HCRST handshake (programmed state wiped, HCRST self-clears,
CNR=0), CONFIG/DCBAAP/CRCR/DNCTRL stores, PORTSC empty-port semantics
(PP=1 under PPC=0, wake bits store, writes fabricate no CCS/PED/
change bits), interrupter-0 ERSTSZ/ERSTBA/ERDP/IMOD/IMAN stores, and
doorbells accepted (the ring engine is X2).  State is plain data and
rides snapshots through xhci_snap ("dev.xhci").

Vectors: tests/test_xhci.c, 9 groups through the real 0xCF8/0xCFC and
MMIO paths, including a miniature replay of the guest's measured
11-step xhci_init (0 devices until X4 binds the sticks).  NC: the
devices.c wiring reverted -> 58 failures (the class scan finds
nothing).

Presence is unconditional (the UHCI-default pattern) and measured
receipt-neutral: make test and make test-sanitize green with every
historical lane byte-identical, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

docs/plans/XHCI_PLAN.md (status + section 1e), docs/STATUS.md,
ROADMAP.md and CHANGELOG.md updated in this commit; patch 0077
follows.
